FFmpeg for NVIDIA drivers older than 610, by the FFmpeg developers and the
authors of the libraries it is built with. Licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3: see LICENSE.txt in the folder it is unpacked in.

Polyfin downloads it, on Linux (amd64, arm64) and Windows (x64), when
NVENC's test encode finds an NVIDIA driver older than 610 that NVENC's API
13.0 takes, into the data folder's tools/nvenc13. It is the FFmpeg of the
Polyfin image, n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068, built with the same recipe against
NVENC's API 13.0 by scripts/ffmpeg-nvenc13.sh and the workflow
ffmpeg-nvenc13, and published as the release
ffmpeg-nvenc13.0-autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08 of
https://github.com/moodiness/polyfin

Its complete corresponding source code is attached to the same release:
ffmpeg-n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068-nvenc13.0-sources.tar, in parts
(.tar.part01, .tar.part02) to join with cat, in order, and to check with
its .tar.sha256. It holds the source of FFmpeg at its commit, of every
library it is built with as the build fetched it, the build recipe, and
how Polyfin adjusted and pinned it (recipe.diff, pins.env).

Polyfin is a separate program, released under the MIT License. It runs
this FFmpeg as a program, as it runs the FFmpeg of its image.
